// Legacy's Any is next's (an alias): the properties it declares are next's code. Read from legacy code, their
// values cross into it, and are legacy's — the loader rewrites legacy code's reads of them into these.

// An object's generic type, as legacy reads it: of the next object a wrapper stands for (next's property
// would describe the wrapper class), adapted.
function meta::pure::bridge::m3::classifierGenericType(x: Any[1]): meta::pure::metamodel::type::generics::GenericType[0..1]
{
   meta::pure::bridge::m3::unwrap($x).classifierGenericType->map(g | meta::pure::bridge::m3::adapt($g))->cast(@meta::pure::metamodel::type::generics::GenericType)
}
